      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-349872",
      ":question/problem": "The elevation of a location is measured relative to height above sea level, in meters. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n| An elevation of $-4m$ means $4$ meters below sea level. | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | ---: |\n| If elevation moves from $-2m$ to $3m$, it increases by $5$ meters. | {{field-2}} |\n| An elevation of $0m$ means \"at sea level.\" | {{field-3}} |"
